                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "233592946",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198044406233",
                            "num_reviews": 108,
                            "playtime_forever": 701,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 430,
                            "last_played": 1789566534
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It has a good foundation, but automatically clearing rows you've completed is very annoying. It's a bit of a slow process and, during the animation, prevents you from making any moves. That's because the playing field changes since it's removing a row and compressing downwards. The game also just forces you to guess at times. I don't know if it's because the row removals, but it doesn't make sense in a game that's supposed to be based in logic.\n\nKept playing a bit more, and the game still sucks. I found out there's a setting that ups the speed of animations, which helps line clearing, but the glaringly obvious issue is still there. You have to guess in this game. The developer even admits this, in a discussion post, and tries to appease people by telling them to utilize the strategy of working the top of the field only and using the bottom for when you're forced to guess. That doesn't fix a damn thing. It got me to 100% difficulty, but then I was forced to guess and the game was over. JUST FIX BOARD GENERATION SO WE'RE NOT FORCED TO GUESS",
